# Article: Pack (four)

Roles: specifier, coder, refactorer, architect.

Chain: specifier -> coder -> refactorer -> architect -> specifier.

- specifier turns a request into an accepted specification, then sends a
  git_handoff to coder.
- coder implements the specified slice, then forwards to refactorer.
- refactorer cleans the implementation, then forwards to architect.
- architect reviews structure and boundaries, then sends the return
  git_handoff to specifier. This return handoff is TERMINAL: specifier
  merges it and stops.
